Based on the true story of the 1868 murder of Laura Foster in North Carolina, allegedly by confederate veteran Tom Dooley.  There are many variations and this one is the version made popular  by the Kingston Trio in 1958.  However, it's rather abbreviated and doesn't tell the full story so there's another version in (G) based on additional lyrics found in traditional lore which paints a more complete picture.

TIP:  The introduction is spoken over the picked (banjo) notes of the chorus.

 
